{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1782256685,"nonce":"/4vNKpLUUNPAQRdwBiHTPfpjhe4=","metadata":{"github-id":"I_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABGfHbTw","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/316","origin":"github"},"title":"RCA: garmin_sidescan range_m appears to affect down-view bottom auto-track (down-view stuck ~1.8 m, recovered by range_m=5) — 2026-06-23 Massabesic","message":"## Summary\n\nDuring the 2026-06-23 Massabesic survey ([#313](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/313)), the garmin_sidescan **down-view (nadir) channel got stuck reporting ~1.8 m max range** (`nadir_depth` max_range ~1.84 m, current return ~0.18 m). Operator observed that **setting the sidescan `range_m` parameter to 5 m got the down-view channel auto-tracking the bottom again.**\n\n## Why this is an RCA\n\nThe field agent (gabby) concluded that `range_m` controls only the sidescan channel and that the down-view cap was independent / device-side, so a `range_m` change \"couldn't\" affect it. **The operator's observation walks that back** — setting `range_m` to 5 m restored down-view bottom auto-tracking, so there *is* a cross-channel interaction (or at least a shared path) between the sidescan `range_m` setting and the down-view channel's auto-range behavior. The mechanism is not understood.\n\n## To investigate\n\n- How does `range_m` on the garmin_sidescan node propagate to the down-view (nadir) channel's ranging/auto-track?\n- Is the ~1.8 m down-view cap a device-side bottom-lock state that a small `range_m` resets, or does the driver gate the down-view on the sidescan range?\n- Document the correct operator action when the down-view stalls (and whether it should be automatic).\n\n## Notes\n\n- `range_m` is a runtime node param (bounds 1.0–60.0 m), not durable across a node relaunch.\n- The driver lives in the garmin_sidescan package (sensors layer) — this may move there once the path is confirmed.\n\n## Evidence\n\ngabby log entries 15:12–15:13 + wrap-up correction, `docs/logs/2026/2026-06-23_gabby_logs.md` (deployment #313). Part of #313.\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context)`","files":null}]}